Thought for 1m 13s

Yes — the right structure is not one big “Calculators” page. It is a hub → category → tool system, exactly like the big calculator sites do. Omni groups calculators into broad topics such as Biology, Chemistry, Construction, Conversion, Finance, Health, Math, Physics, Sports, and more, and then goes deeper into sub-topics inside each category; Calculator.net does the same with themed sections like Fitness & Health containing many tools under one umbrella. Omni also explicitly says its mission is to solve small real-life problems shared by millions.

